# PWA and caching

- Keep **app-shell** caching separate from large **playa-pack** and **map** storage.
- Version cache names and pack formats (`src/lib/pwa/versioning.ts`: shell, pack format, sample data).
- Never casually cache authenticated **mutation** responses as source of truth.
- Service-worker updates must **not** delete pending local user data (IndexedDB / outbox).
- Test upgrades from an existing cached version when changing SW or precache strategy.
- Do not add broad caching rules without documenting scope and invalidation in `docs/offline-strategy.md`.
- Incomplete pack downloads must not activate for Explore / map use.
- Recommended toolchain: `vite-plugin-pwa` (Workbox) — **in use** for app-shell precache; keep pack/map caches separate and versioned.
- First meaningful paint of the shell must not require Supabase.
